From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Botond Lovasz <botilovasz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:51:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Run ConfigMap hooks around GPU driver switches

--vfio-switch-hooks-configmap names a ConfigMap in the plugin's namespace.
On every driver switch, its entries "unbound.<name>" run with no driver
bound and "bound.<name>" after the target driver is bound, in key order,
as shell scripts with PCI_ADDRESS and DRIVER (the target) set. A failing
hook fails the switch. Empty (the default): no hooks.

This keeps host-specific steps out of the driver. On RTX 3090s, FLR
sometimes leaves the card's firmware unbooted (RmInitAdapter 0x62:0x65);
a secondary bus reset from the "unbound" stage recovers it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
